{
  "slug": "artist:plump-djs",
  "name": "Plump DJs",
  "editorial_article": "London duo Lee Rous and Andy Gardner helped establish the breakbeat sound in the late 1990s after meeting at the west London label Freskanova. Their debut 1999 release, \"Plump Chunks/Electric Disco,\" launched their presence on Finger Lickin' Records, a label that would host much of their early work. The pair gained international visibility through mix compilations like the 2001 Mixmag cover CD Elastic Breaks and the 2003 FabricLive 08 entry, which coincided with a decade-long residency at London's Fabric club. Their 2003 artist album Eargasm featured vocal contributions from Louise Rhodes and synth-work by Gary Numan. In 2010, the duo founded their own imprint, Grand Hotel, which they used to release their later material, including the single \"My Hi Tops\" and collaborations such as \"You Belong to Us\" with singer Juliette Ashby. Their live shows evolved to feature a four-deck performance technique, allowing for complex arrangements that they brought to festivals including Coachella and Glastonbury. Throughout their career, they have provided remix work for artists such as deadmau5, Fatboy Slim, and Orbital.",
